X-OMNE-FIXTURE-NOTE:Reproduces omne_harness/requirements/intake/business-
 calendar-source-research/us-calendar-source-dossier.md measured shapes
 (2026-08-19): observed-only DTSTART dates; SUMMARY apostrophe codepoints
 mixed inside one file (U+0027 in 2021-2023 blocks and Washington's
 Birthday 2025, U+2019 in 2024+ blocks); 2021-12-31 cross-year New Year
 spillover; 2025-01-20 dual VEVENT (MLK + Inauguration Day); Inauguration
 Day present 2021/2025 only. Dates computed from 6103(a)/(b)(1)+EO 11582
 rules and cross-checked against dossier appendix A per-year counts and
 the verbatim 2026 list.
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20260818T212045Z
UID:fixture-20210101-28059@opm.gov
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20210101
SUMMARY:New Year's Day
DESCRIPTION:If a holiday falls on a Saturday, for most Federal employees, 
 the preceding Friday will be treated as a holiday for pay and leave purpo
 ses. (See 5 U.S.C. 6103(b).) If a holiday falls on a Sunday, for most Fed
 eral employees, the following Monday will be treated as a holiday for pay
  and leave purposes. (See Section 3(a) of Executive Order 11582, February
  11, 1971.) See also https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/pay-leave/
 federal-holidays/tabs/2021/
END:VEVENT
